/*
  PDFRender - baseline TIFF decoding.  See h/pdftiff.

  Written from the TIFF 6.0 specification.  A TIFF is a header
  pointing at a directory of tagged fields, which in turn point at the
  pixels; the fields may be in either byte order and the pixels may be
  in strips or tiles, so most of the work here is reading the
  directory carefully and then walking whichever layout it describes.

